# Density Compare
# Titanium (Ti) — real density 4.506 g/cm³. equal masses: Titanium vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Titanium Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 12.1mm material: titanium at (-20mm, 6.0mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 35.9 g — the water cube is the reference
